WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.880
David, do you think Washington, DC s strict
gun laws saved?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.340
Lives during the Trump riot.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.740
This is a very interesting question.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.299
It's really a question that has to be thought
about in large numbers.

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:20.560
And what I mean by that is, statistically,
DC s gun laws almost certainly saved some

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.960
lives.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.690
Let me talk talk through my sense of it.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.230
And if you disagree with me, just let me know.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:34.220
I know that the gun people often say gun laws
don't stop any crimes because the criminals

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.330
don't follow the laws anyway, the criminals
will find an illegal way to get a gun.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.020
The criminals will bring guns where they aren't
allowed anyway.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.580
So it doesn't make a difference.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.230
And certainly anecdotally, that may well be
true to some degree.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.850
That may well be true.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:58.520
But there are certainly some insurrectionists
who opted to leave their firearms at home

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:06.660
who, if the laws were laxer in D.C., would
have brought guns with them.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.060
Some of them certainly had guns with them.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.630
We know that.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:16.430
But the number of guns was certainly lower
because of Washington, DC s gun laws.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:22.650
As a result of that, there are certainly some
people who, if they had had firearms with

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:31.100
them on that day in Washington, D.C., could
have been ending up in some kind of a confrontation

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:37.620
where either they would have taken outdrawn
or used their firearm or police may have used

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.370
one against them by virtue of seeing that
some of these individuals were armed.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.760
So were there people in the Capitol with guns?

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.760
Probably.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.100
Yeah, probably they were some.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.620
Would the number have been higher?

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.020
Were the gun laws way more relaxed in Washington,
D.C.?

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.560
Yeah, I think it's undeniable that more people
would have had guns and reducing the number

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:03.799
of guns in the situation removes lowers the
probability that there would have been more

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:05.260
of an escalation.

